**playstation.hpp switches PlayStation Bluetooth controllers to extended HID reports and identifies minimal-mode reports.**

## Interface

`enable_extended_reports(const context&, transport::hid_device&, device_id, family) noexcept` performs Bluetooth feature exchange; returns whether a feature report was read, gating extended-report driver binding.

`minimal_bluetooth_report(span<const byte>, connection) noexcept` detects the 10-byte `0x01` minimal report and enables silent dropping.

## Contracts

`enable_extended_reports` is unnecessary over USB; extended formats are DualSense `0x31` and DualShock 4 `0x11`. Dependencies: `types.hpp`, `utility.hpp`, `context`, `device_id`, `transport::hid_device`.